    {
      "id": "M-C6-N1-SCENE",
      "note": "N1-master-cam-02 (right-hand fist corrected) placed in cliffside_v21 as prop necro_master_still (3840,720) via CS-props-v21; Keeper walk-around + 4 stills captured → Desktop Packet 86; sent to Matt. C-6 STOPS here pending the master decision (no turnaround/loops until ruled).",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T19:43:11"
    },
    {
      "id": "M-C6-N2-SCYTHE",
      "note": "N2-master-scythe-01 DELIVERED_WITH_CONCERNS (2 image calls; sha c285c523…): scythe baked into the accepted master — haft through both existing fists (upper wrap in the raised right fist, lower wrap in the hip-level left fist), blade upper-left curving outward clear of the face, butt-spike lower-right above the ground line; figure feet line unchanged (y 1010), horn on his left shoulder; composite bbox h 897 px (blade adds ~190 px above the head). Conductor eye: PASS on every retry criterion. Awaiting Matt's eye (charter § 5 F5) + fork rulings F1–F4. C-6 charter DRAFT v0.1 filed.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:06:17"
    },
    {
      "id": "M-C6-N2-R1",
      "note": "N2-master-scythe-r1 DELIVERED (1 image call): real-scythe proportions — weapon 1.13× figure height overall, blade head narrower than the shoulders, tip ~90 px above the head; both fists on the wraps; figure unchanged. Model returned a TRANSPARENT (RGBA) plate instead of green — conductor composited a green-plate copy for the lane (necro_master_scythe_r1_green.png). Awaiting Matt's eye.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:12:25"
    },
    {
      "id": "M-C6-N2-R2",
      "note": "N2-master-scythe-r2 DELIVERED (2 image calls) against a TOOLING-PLACED GUIDE (scythe_guide_r2.png: design keyed, scaled to haft 550 px = 0.78 H, rotated 56.5° onto the fist line, placed through both fists): straight haft, blade beside the right shoulder, butt-spike past the hip fist, composite bbox h 707 = figure height (nothing above the head), figure pixels unchanged. Lesson (Astra S1 § 2b confirmed on a character): size/angle/position are a tooling contract, not prose. Awaiting Matt's eye.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:31:14"
    }
  ],
  "halts": [],
  "rulings": [
    {
      "id": "R-C6-0",
      "class": "matt",
      "veto_open": false,
      "ts": "2026-09-15T22:50:23Z",
      "ruling": "Character 2 = end-game Necromancer. Matt: text-designed (Blizzard render = design read only, never attached); grip classes accepted (2H-polearm / 1H+off-hand / empty caster; weapons as socketed layers; scythe = a layer); STOP after the master until Matt decides it. Matt generated the DESIGN master in the ChatGPT app (first-party) — camera at eye level; Matt: \"take my image and prompt around it to reach the size / angle\" → N1-master-cam-01 re-mints at the scene camera with the Keeper rest frame as IMAGE 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "R-C6-1",
      "class": "matt",
      "veto_open": false,
      "ruling": "Matt (verbatim): 'I like the Necro as master copy. I think we will need him to hold the scythe for now.' → N1-master-cam-02 ACCEPTED as the C-6 design master. Scythe: in-hand for the first animation set (the grip-class weapon-layer split stays as direction, deferred); composition method pending Matt's word on the conductor lean (bake the scythe into the master before the turnaround/loops, as the Keeper's staff is).",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T19:50:22"
    },
    {
      "id": "R-C6-2",
      "class": "matt",
      "veto_open": false,
      "ruling": "Fork 1 — Matt: 'bake it in.' The scythe is composited into the accepted master (two-handed polearm grip) and that composite is the animation master for the turnaround + loops; the weapon-layer split stays as filed direction.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:02:25"
    },
    {
      "id": "R-C6-3",
      "class": "matt",
      "veto_open": false,
      "ruling": "Fork 2 — Matt: 'we won't need a following lap.. but maybe in the future.' The unarmed (empty-caster) master state + idle/walk set is NOT scheduled; parked as a future lap. C-6 scope = scythe-in-hand set only.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:02:25"
    },
    {
      "id": "R-C6-4",
      "class": "matt",
      "veto_open": false,
      "ruling": "N2-master-scythe-01 FAILS Matt's eye (charter F5): 'The scythe is completely the wrong size.. it needs to be fit down to size of a real scythe.' Conductor fault: the N2 brief specified haft ≈ figure height + blade above it (≈ 1.3× his height overall, blade ≈ 0.5× height). N2-r1 re-mints from the ORIGINAL master with real-scythe proportions: haft ≈ 0.85× figure height (≈ 600 px), blade chord ≈ 0.35× figure height (≈ 250 px), blade head no wider than his shoulders, tip no higher than one head above him.",
      "ts": "2026-09-15T20:09:28"
    },
    {
      "id": "R-C6-5",
